139:  Asymmetry constraint: you have only the diff and the plan. You do not have my reasoning for any specific decision. If something looks wrong, flag it - I will dismiss what is intentional. Report what you find; the blocking threshold below decides which findings block.
140:
141:  Blocking threshold: report every finding you can substantiate, but mark it a blocker only when a realistic trigger leads to it and the result (a) breaks the goal, the value proof, a `## Merge gate` criterion, or an existing consumer - of the change, or of the plan when you review one - or (b) reaches a protected asset. A realistic trigger is normal use, input or state that occurs in ordinary operation, or an actor outside the trust boundary sending plausible input; a state the user would have to construct deliberately on their own machine (corrupted or permission-stripped local files, hand-inserted NUL bytes, racing manual runs) is not one. A gap that appears only for an input variant the change does not claim to handle (an alternative syntax or layout) and whose damage stays in the user's own environment and is reversible is a note, not a blocker. Work the plan excludes that the change implements anyway is a blocker without a trigger. A protected asset is production data, a real credential, third-party personal data, tenant isolation, money, an audit trail, or irreversible state; a local development default in the developer's own environment is not one. Weakening access to a protected asset counts even when no data moves. Judge by causation, not location: a defect the change causes or exposes in unchanged code counts; a pre-existing defect the change neither causes nor exposes is a note. Each blocker starts a line with `Blocker B<n>:` (numbered from B1 in order) and names its trigger, preconditions, impact, and whether the damage is reversible. A finding whose precondition already grants what exploiting it would gain is not a blocker. Every other finding is a note with one line on why it does not block. A false note costs nothing; a false blocker costs a fix wave.
